The parent class owns the shared state and accessor and declares the behaviour that varies as abstract methods. Each concrete game only implements what differs. The factory is a single `if/elif` chain over the enum, so callers depend on `BoardGame` and `GameType` only. Adding a new game means one new class and one new branch.

